    value: {"single": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0.05}, {"over": 1083150, "rate": 0.09}], "mfj": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0.05}, {"over": 1083150, "rate": 0.09}], "mfs": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0.05}, {"over": 1083150, "rate": 0.09}], "hoh": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0.05}, {"over": 1083150, "rate": 0.09}], "qss": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0.05}, {"over": 1083150, "rate": 0.09}], "simplified": true, "note": "Flat 5.00% on Part B (wages, most income), Part A interest/dividends and Part C long-term gains, plus 4% surtax on total taxable income over the threshold -> modelled as 9% bracket. Threshold is the SAME for every filing status (not doubled for joint returns; each MFS return has its own threshold). simplified=true because the surtax applies to ALL taxable income including short-term gains (taxed 8.5% -> 12.5% above threshold) and collectibles (12%), which a single bracket cannot capture. No HOH/QSS-specific rate (flat)."},
