    citation: "Missouri DOR, 2025 Form MO-1040 Instructions, https://dor.mo.gov/forms/MO-1040%20Instructions_2025.pdf, Form MO-A Line 18 instructions (p.15): 'The state of Missouri allows a subtraction from your federal adjusted gross income for 100 percent of your federally reported capital gains. Enter the amount of capital gains reported on your Federal Form 1040 or 1040-SR, Line 7a ... If the amount reported on your Federal Form 1040 or 1040-SR, Line 7a was negative, enter $0'. Statute RSMo 143.121.3(14)(a), https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=143.121 : 'For all tax years beginning on or after January 1, 2025, one hundred percent of all income reported as a capital gain for federal income tax purposes by an individual'. (2026: statute continues; CARRIED FORWARD of form-line mechanics since 2026 MO-A not yet published as of 2026-10-13.)",
