    citation: "2026 Oregon Estimated Income Tax Instructions (Publication OR-ESTIMATE, 150-101-026), 'Estimated Oregon indexed figures for tax year 2026', https://www.oregon.gov/dor/forms/FormsPubs/publication-or-estimate_101-026_2026.pdf: 'Federal tax subtraction: $0 to $8,750'; worksheet line 9 'Federal tax liability ($0 to $8,750).*' '* The federal tax subtraction phases out above certain federal AGI levels.' Tier structure: ORS 316.695(1)(c)(A)-(B) federal income tax subtraction (official text https://www.oregonlegislature.gov/bills_laws/ors/ors316.html; read via oregon.public.law mirror): base limit for AGI < $125,000 ($250,000 joint) reduced to 80%/60%/40%/20% in $5,000 ($10,000 joint) steps, zero at $145,000 ($290,000 joint); limit indexed, rounded down to $50.",
