    value: {"single": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0}, {"over": 3560, "rate": 0.03}, {"over": 17830, "rate": 0.06}], "mfj": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0}, {"over": 3560, "rate": 0.03}, {"over": 17830, "rate": 0.06}], "mfs": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0}, {"over": 3560, "rate": 0.03}, {"over": 17830, "rate": 0.06}], "hoh": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0}, {"over": 3560, "rate": 0.03}, {"over": 17830, "rate": 0.06}], "qss": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0}, {"over": 3560, "rate": 0.03}, {"over": 17830, "rate": 0.06}], "simplified": true, "note": "One schedule for all filing statuses. Thresholds $3,560/$17,830 are not printed on the 2025 return materials (schedule for $100,000+ is '6% minus $642'); they come from the 2025 SC1040ES/WH-1603F schedule (which still shows the old 6.2% top rate) and are CONFIRMED against the 2025 tax table: 3,600-3,650 -> $2 ((3,625-3,560)x3%=1.95); 17,900-18,000 -> $435 (428.10+120x6%=435.3); 50,000-50,100 -> $2,361 (6%x50,050-641.70=2,361.3); constant: 6%xTI - (3%x3,560 + 3%x17,830) = 6%xTI - 641.70, i.e. the published $642. Tax table midpoint rounding not modelled."},
    citation: "2025 South Carolina Individual Income Tax Tables (Revised 6/17/25), https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/SC1040TT_2025.pdf: '2025 Tax Rate Schedule for taxable income of $100,000 or more ... Use this Tax Rate Schedule for any filing status ... 1. Multiply the amount on line 5 by 6%; 2. Subtract $642'; tax table rows '3,600 3,650 $2', '17,900 18,000 $435', '50,000 50,100 $2,361' (consistent with 0% to $3,560, 3% to $17,830, 6% above). Bracket thresholds per 2025 SC1040ES (https://dor.sc.gov/forms-site/Forms/SC1040ES_2025.pdf).",
