    value: {"standard_deduction": 278000, "brackets": [{"over": 0, "rate": 0.07}, {"over": 1000000, "rate": 0.099}], "estimates_required": false, "note": "Same structure as 2025: 7% on Washington capital gains up to $1,000,000 after the standard deduction, 9.9% (7% + 2.9%) above. Long-term gains only. Estimated/quarterly payments NOT required; new optional prepayment window (up to 6 months before the April 15, 2027 due date). Same late-payment / substantial-underpayment (<80% paid by due date) penalty rules under ch. 82.32 RCW. The 2026 standard deduction stored here is the 2025 figure carried forward - replace when DOR publishes. Separately, the 2026 Legislature enacted a new WA income tax on high earners (reported March 2026); it does not change the capital gains excise tax for 2025/2026 and was not researched here. Measured on: 'Washington capital gains' (RCW 82.87.020(16)) = federal net LONG-TERM capital gain, adjusted (add back certain LT losses; subtract exempt / non-Washington-allocated gains, RCW 82.87.050/.100), then reduced by the RCW 82.87.060 deductions - the standard deduction (per individual, married couple or domestic partnership - one deduction per return, not doubled for joint), charitable deduction over the threshold, qualified family-owned small business deduction, etc. The $1,000,000 tier and both rates apply to that amount AFTER the standard deduction; the $1M threshold is not indexed. Short-term gains are not taxed. Exempt asset classes (e.g. real estate, retirement accounts) are listed in RCW 82.87.050 - not modelled. Due with the return 2027-04-15."},
